     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.	Scale-2- Very Partially (SDGs integrated in the mandate of existing coordination structures, but no new structures established)
1.2. Scale-2- Partially (SDG frameworks at national/sub-national level established but planning tools are not SDGs aligned) 
1.3-Scale-3- Moderate: (Stakeholders have decent understanding of SDGs)
1.4-Scale-2 - Very Partially- (Private sector very partially engaged in SDG implementation) 
2.1- Scale-3- Partially (Baselines and targets established for prioritized SDG indicators)
2.2-Scale-2- Very Partially (Little understanding and knowledge to effectively report and monitor progress on SDGs)
3.1-Scale-2 &#x2013; Partially (Performance based criteria established but not fully used for resource allocation at national/ sub-national level)
3.2-Scale-2 &#x2013; Partially (frameworks/MIS capacity established for effective aid coordination)
3.3-Scale-2 &#x2013; Partially (Results based, and inclusive processes partially inform budget allocation at national and sub national level)
4.1-Scale-2 &#x2013; Partially (Innovative approaches fully established for SDG acceleration)</narrative>
      </comment>
